{"at":"2026-11-05T11:41:46.188644+00:00","items":[{"detail":"Alaska voters approved Measure 2, replacing party primaries with a nonpartisan jungle primary where the top four candidates advance to a general election using instant-runoff voting.","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","party":"","scope":"statewide","source":"wikipedia","state":"AK","status":"adopted","system":"Top-four/Final-five + RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","year":"2020"},{"detail":"Instant\u2011runoff voting was used in Alaska's at\u2011large congressional district special election in 2022.","model":"openai/gpt-oss-20b","party":"","scope":"congressional","source":"wikipedia","state":"AK","status":"in use","system":"RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instant-runoff_voting","year":"2022"},{"detail":"Another measure seeking to repeal the ranked-choice voting system gathered enough signatures to appear on Alaska ballots in 2026.","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","party":"","scope":"statewide","source":"wikipedia","state":"AK","status":"petition drive","system":"Top-four/Final-five + RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","year":"2026"},{"detail":"A measure to repeal the ranked-choice voting system and return to partisan primaries narrowly failed by a margin of 737 votes.","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","party":"","scope":"statewide","source":"wikipedia","state":"AK","status":"rejected","system":"Top-four/Final-five + RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","year":"2024"},{"detail":"Arkansas allows absentee voters to submit ranked ballots in runoff elections.","model":"openai/gpt-oss-20b","party":"","scope":"statewide","source":"wikipedia","state":"AR","status":"in use","system":"RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instant-runoff_voting","year":""},{"detail":"Instant\u2011runoff voting was used in the 2010 elections in Oakland, San Francisco and San Leandro, California.","model":"openai/gpt-oss-20b","party":"","scope":"local","source":"wikipedia","state":"CA","status":"in use","system":"RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instant-runoff_voting","year":"2010"},{"detail":"The District of Columbia voted for Initiative 83, which will implement ranked-choice voting in all presidential, federal, and district elections by 2026.","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","party":"","scope":"statewide","source":"wikipedia","state":"DC","status":"adopted","system":"RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","year":"2024"},{"detail":"Hawaii Governor David Ige signed Senate Bill 2162 into law allowing for the use of instant-runoff voting for the special election of federal and county council offices.","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","party":"","scope":"congressional","source":"wikipedia","state":"HI","status":"adopted","system":"RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","year":"2022"},{"detail":"Springfield, Illinois allows absentee voters to submit ranked ballots in runoff elections.","model":"openai/gpt-oss-20b","party":"","scope":"local","source":"wikipedia","state":"IL","status":"in use","system":"RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instant-runoff_voting","year":""},{"detail":"Louisiana uses ranked ballots for absentee voters in runoff elections only for members of the U.S. Service or overseas residents.","model":"openai/gpt-oss-20b","party":"","scope":"statewide","source":"wikipedia","state":"LA","status":"in use","system":"RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instant-runoff_voting","year":""},{"detail":"The Maine Legislature passed a bill adopting instant-runoff voting for both presidential primaries and the general election, which became law in September 2019.","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","party":"","scope":"presidential primary","source":"wikipedia","state":"ME","status":"adopted","system":"RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","year":"2019"},{"detail":"Instant-runoff voting was retained for the 2020 U.S. Senate and U.S. House elections after a court rejected arguments that it was unconstitutional.","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","party":"","scope":"statewide","source":"wikipedia","state":"ME","status":"in use","system":"RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","year":"2020"},{"detail":"The Maine Republican Party's attempt to qualify a veto referendum to repeal the instant-runoff voting law failed after the secretary of state rejected insufficient signatures, a decision upheld by the Maine Supreme Judicial Court.","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","party":"Republican","scope":"presidential primary","source":"wikipedia","state":"ME","status":"rejected","system":"RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","year":"2020"},{"detail":"South Carolina allows absentee voters to submit ranked ballots in runoff elections.","model":"openai/gpt-oss-20b","party":"","scope":"statewide","source":"wikipedia","state":"SC","status":"in use","system":"RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instant-runoff_voting","year":""},{"detail":"Utah passed a law allowing municipalities to opt in to a temporary instant-runoff voting trial starting with the 2019 municipal elections and ending with the 2025 elections.","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","party":"","scope":"local","source":"wikipedia","state":"UT","status":"adopted","system":"RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","year":"2018"},{"detail":"The Virginia legislature passed a bill providing a local option for municipalities to use the single transferable vote through 2031.","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","party":"","scope":"local","source":"wikipedia","state":"VA","status":"adopted","system":"RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","year":"2020"},{"detail":"Seattle adopted ranked-choice voting for its primary elections after voters chose it over approval voting.","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","party":"","scope":"local","source":"wikipedia","state":"WA","status":"in use","system":"RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","year":""}],"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Approval_voting","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Approval_voting","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/STAR_voting","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electoral_reform_in_the_United_States","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instant-runoff_voting","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instant-runoff_voting","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instant-runoff_voting","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instant-runoff_voting","https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijAFBVV95cUxQWHR2VXB0Tkw0ODVrNnYtb0M2RGVHR3hMNURUeVIzRjMxdThKb1ZjeHNhUjY4Y0ZTTzhLOV84eXg1MnhZOEhydF9aeDJyRDFXLWZsSnJqbFY0Z2hkMW1CTnV6VGhhcmpqeTNwOUkxN2JhRXotUFM4WHg3ZUFETDFEQW1PdjczUU9kRUpqZA?oc=5","https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqgFBVV95cUxNS0x0LVVNbnZhQm1MZi1yX0RMU1k4c2JBTWR4cFJxdlJvZmpFVEdObU5YaENueXJCT1ZpeDhWQkdxWW1uXzJRTDEwalhSdjBuQk82UHoxcHVlTDE3OEdtWExwQ3pkRGRLdFdTOGhyazJOQWg2T0pIUVBIMXdKNW1UWDhtU1pUSjR5OW5TRFZLbURGNlAwNXAtSXE1bG42RkRGYkxBY2dRNFNmdw?oc=5","https://news.google.?oc=5","https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivAFBVV95cUxPVnRrSVBpR2EtcEljRFIyM05sWVFwTGY3VU5mbjl6Yl9oUzNQQXZuY3Q0Tldza29NekNxLWNscktzVkRKbFVuWUstUnRmcnFTNnZ6cHZrZFFDTk83WDdoQXhwemVlM3RpbXNkdUZWZ1BxQm9LbkZYclBVMlJqcGpsZ240alB3NC1oVEdPNW9IaC1teFJjZUtVaWY3S3d5UGVnaGViNlRrcTIybFVCeE1NV0xlel84N1kxZ2tMNQ?oc=5","https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilwFBVV95cUxQcTZzOW9DMnRIRTF5TlFtTWZ2TDYyREJtV0d0Z1lxcl9rMmtSRkM4SmJKQmlGbV9PdFFRM